union-rebase-duplicates-the-ledger	0x007FFB50	0	tooling	A REBASE CAN SILENTLY DUPLICATE THOUSANDS OF LEDGER ROWS and the fix is not to repair the result. functions.csv merges with a union driver, so `git rebase` onto a moved origin/master appended the incoming rows wholesale: 161896 rows became 167328, i.e. 5432 duplicates, in a commit whose own pre-commit gate had just passed. Only the PRE-PUSH check_csv caught it. tools/dedup_csv.py then REFUSED, correctly, because the debris included one address claimed by two different sources - and that pair was stale: origin/master had exactly one owner for it while my base still carried an earlier spelling of the same conversion, and the union kept both. THE CHEAP AND CORRECT MOVE IS TO REDO THE WORK ON TOP OF origin/master rather than to dedup: reset hard, restore the source file and the pin, re-run add_match_batch. That rewrites functions.csv from a clean base and cannot resurrect anything. Deduping instead would have made me arbitrate an ownership conflict that was never mine.
boolean-spelling-is-visible-in-bytes	0x007FF3F0	52	tooling	FOUR SPELLINGS OF ONE BOOLEAN FUNCTION, ALL CORRECT, ALL DIFFERENT IN BYTES - worth keeping because the search order is reusable. Retail 0x007FF3F0 is an ordinary leap-year test. (1) STATEMENT FORM vs EXPRESSION FORM decides the RETURN WIDTH: an if/else with explicit returns sets al, while a bare return over the same condition materialises an int and sets eax. (2) ONE CONDITION vs SEVERAL STATEMENTS decides TAIL SHARING: a single short-circuit condition gives one shared true tail and one shared false tail, while a chain of if-returns duplicates a tail per branch, and MSVC then folds the last two-constant branch into neg/sbb/inc arithmetic instead of a jump. THE COMBINATION THAT MATCHED IS BOTH AT ONCE: one expression inside an if/else with explicit returns. (3) THE GROUPING IS READ FROM THE JUMP TARGETS, not assumed: when the divisible-by-four test FAILS, retail jumps to the divisible-by-400 test rather than to false, which refutes the textbook grouping (which can only reach the 400 test after the 4 test passes) and identifies the equivalent regrouping. (4) AT THE CALL SITE, adding a bool straight to an int gives movzx eax,al, which trusts the callee; an explicit ternary emits the neg/sbb/neg normalisation retail has. ALSO: the constructor initially INLINED its own setter. /Ob1 is what stops that, and a TU whose bodies call each other out-of-line is evidence for /Ob1 over default auto-inlining.
byte-exact-but-wrong-purpose	0x007FDEE0	225	note	A CONVERSION THAT WAS BYTE-EXACT AND STILL DESCRIBED THE WRONG THING, corrected by a caller. 0x007FDEE0 was landed earlier as an address-translator ROUND-TRIP SELF TEST, and in isolation that is exactly what it looks like: build one socket address for 192.168.1.1 port 79, push it through the translator at 0x007FE310, read the address back out. Nothing in the body says otherwise. Its caller does: the comm transport at 0x00816160 calls it with no arguments and stores the result as the connection's LOCAL ADDRESS, beside a local port read from a bind query. It is LOCAL ADDRESS DISCOVERY - the translator is a routing query, so asking which interface would be used to reach an outside address and KEEPING the answer rather than comparing it is how you learn your own address without enumerating interfaces. 0xC0A80101 is not a test vector, it is a plausible LAN gateway. THE GENERAL POINT: THE BYTE GATE CANNOT CHECK WHAT A BODY IS FOR. A green row with a confident wrong purpose in its comment is worse than an unconverted one, because the next reader inherits it. Where a body has no strings and no obvious side effect, treat the purpose as PROVISIONAL until a caller is converted, and say so.
